        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nick Cave, Mick Harvey, Blixa Bargeld, Eddie White, Ari Gibson\n- Bands: Grinderman, Nick Cave and the Bad Seeds\n- Albums and Songs: Grinderman, \"No Pussy Blues\"\n- Films: The Cat Piano\n- Companies and Labels: Mute Records, ANTI-\n- Places: Melbourne, Europe, United States\n\nFacts:\n- Nick Cave and the Bad Seeds are an Australian rock band formed in Melbourne in 1983 by Nick Cave, Mick Harvey, and Blixa Bargeld.\n- Grinderman is an alternative rock band that is a side project of members of Nick Cave and the Bad Seeds.\n- Grinderman is the eponymous debut studio album by Grinderman.\n- Grinderman was released on March 5, 2007, on Mute Records in Europe and on ANTI- in the United States.\n- \"No Pussy Blues\" is the second single by Grinderman from the band's debut album Grinderman.\n- The Cat Piano is an award-winning animated short film directed by Eddie White and Ari Gibson and narrated by Nick Cave.\n- The Cat Piano is not to be confused with Keyboard Cat.",
